From 635c0c7bc8c187a92cfcd589aedca9a1597b0efd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:20:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(2d): axis start reseats to an exact edge; XY arc entry
 tries the closing edge

axis_reseat kept the ring start for a first edge within axis_tol, but
only an exact axis edge posts a G18/G19. The start now stays only on an
exact edge, or when no edge is nearer an axis.

plan_xy tried one tangent, from the fitted walk arc. The ring that
returns to the start sat a fraction of a micron off that tangent and
crossed the arc hull at each radius. When no radius fits, the direction
of the closing edge of the first ring is tried, within 1e-3 rad only.

Removes the known-fail #2849 markers of two lead_approach pins. The fig8
ring order pin (shoulder_adaptive) keeps its marker.

Refs #2849

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
